{"uid":"fbc80c977a730094","name":"test_status_json_exits_0_on_the_tier_breakdown_run_with_docker_removed","fullName":"tests.test_status_docker_removed_from_path_task026#test_status_json_exits_0_on_the_tier_breakdown_run_with_docker_removed","historyId":"ecdbb2be761cb2be2f21f6a8710fc739","time":{"start":1791946316119,"stop":1791946316268,"duration":149},"description":"Task 080/085's exact first named node\n    (`test_ralphctl_status_json_exposes_the_tier_bucket`'s own fixture),\n    re-driven the same way. The tier breakdown itself has nothing to do\n    with container liveness, so it must be unaffected; `containerLiveness`\n    is asserted to be the undecided reading (`CONTAINER_LIVENESS_UNKNOWN`,\n    i.e. `\"unknown\"`) that task 026 (E.4) requires of a liveness probe with\n    no docker client to ask -- distinct from `\"absent\"`, which is docker's\n    own answer about a container it looked for and did not find. The\n    narrower `containerGone` field stays False for it (nothing established\n    that anything vanished), while the condition itself is still reported\n    (`dangling` true: a non-terminal run whose API is unreachable and whose\n    engine could not be confirmed alive).","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 080/085's exact first named node<br />\n(<code>test_ralphctl_status_json_exposes_the_tier_bucket</code>'s own fixture),<br />\nre-driven the same way. The tier breakdown itself has nothing to do<br />\nwith container liveness, so it must be unaffected; <code>containerLiveness</code><br />\nis asserted to be the undecided reading (<code>CONTAINER_LIVENESS_UNKNOWN</code>,<br />\ni.e. <code>&quot;unknown&quot;</code>) that task 026 (E.4) requires of a liveness probe with<br />\nno docker client to ask -- distinct from <code>&quot;absent&quot;</code>, which is docker's<br />\nown answer about a container it looked for and did not find. The<br />\nnarrower <code>containerGone</code> field stays False for it (nothing established<br />\nthat anything vanished), wh